<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina to liquidate reinsurance body --report.</title>
<headline>Argentina to liquidate reinsurance body --report.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's President Carlos Menem said Economy Minister Roque Fernandez had signed a resolution to liquidate the National Reinsurance Institute (INDER), the private DyN news agency reported on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Menem told a meeting of insurance company executives that the government would pay off $150 million of INDER's debt over the next 60 days, and the remaining $900 million over five months, according to DyN.</p>
<p>-- Patrick Adam, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0654</p>
